cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use skylakegrep in academic or published work, please cite it as below."
title: "skylakegrep: fully-offline semantic search over local files"
abstract: >-
  skylakegrep is a command-line semantic search tool that runs entirely on
  the local machine. It builds a local SQLite vector index over code,
  markdown, PDFs, Word documents, and plain text, and answers
  natural-language queries in 100+ languages with line-cited snippets. A
  query router chooses between lexical, location-scoped, and semantic
  retrieval routes and reports the route it took; a pluggable extractor
  registry keeps retrieval content-agnostic. Embeddings and optional answer
  synthesis are served by a local Ollama instance, so no file contents, no
  queries, and no telemetry leave the machine. Retrieval accuracy and
  latency are tracked by a committed benchmark harness rather than asserted.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Tianchi"
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-08-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielchen26/skylakegrep"
url: "https://danielchen26.github.io/skylakegrep/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - semantic-search
  - information-retrieval
  - local-first
  - offline
  - embeddings
  - vector-search
  - command-line-tool
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - ollama
  - code-search
